title: What is known about going back over a graph with no task in hand is one note, one request away.
pid: a203b07a-8d05-4797-9f82-3f00b48d7f9d
body: |2-
  Open it before tending a graph, before proposing that anyone dream,
  and before judging whether a rewriting made a graph better:
  [[id:797628ed-c9fb-4a08-8922-d59eb854eed5][Going back over a graph with no task in hand helps when it moves, links and checks claims against their sources, and harms when it rewrites; only probes answered from the graph before and after can tell better from merely different.]]
  Its sources are a group in the note on what I read, and the test it
  proposes is [[id:acc8c677-9169-43ab-9bc2-e14c190d6442][the probe test of a tending, step by step]].
